+# Thanks, Computer
+
+> Deploy Nitro apps to [Thanks, Computer](https://www.thanks.computer).
+
+**Preset:** `thanks-computer` (server), `thanks-computer-static` (prerendered)
+
+:read-more{title="Thanks, Computer" to="https://www.thanks.computer"}
+
+A build is a Web ABI directory, `txco-web/`:
+
+- `public/`, the static output, served by the platform before your app runs;
+- `server/`, the app as a Fetch handler (`thanks-computer` only);
+- `ops/`, the rules that answer what no file does: a page that doesn't exist
+  gets `404.html` with 404, or, for an app rendered in the browser, the app
+  shell with 200;
+- `txco-web.json`, the manifest.
+
+## Deploy a prerendered site
+
+```bash
+npx nitro build --preset thanks-computer-static
+```
+
+Bind the build to a stack in your workspace's `txco.yaml`, then deploy with
+the [txco CLI](https://www.thanks.computer):
+
+```yaml
+stacks:
+  web:
+    abi: txco-web
+```
+
+```bash
+txco web check txco-web
+txco apply
+```
+
+## Deploy a server build
+
+```bash
+npx nitro build --preset thanks-computer
+txco apply --static-only
+```
+
+`--static-only` deploys `public/` and `ops/` until the platform runs the
+`server/` half.
+
+## Options
+
+```ts
+export default defineNitroConfig({
+  thanksComputer: {
+    // Force the browser-rendered app shell for unknown pages (detected for Nuxt `ssr: false`).
+    spa: true,
+    // public/ prefixes cached for a year (derived from `publicAssets` when unset).
+    immutable: ["assets/"],
+  },
+});
+```
